  "sent_to_model": "Can you help me reply to a young person on a jobs forum? They've said they're not enthusiastic and want a job with very little contact with people. I'd like to ask about further education and suggest inexpensive study in something that interests them. I also think they could work on themselves and try something that makes them interact more; my friend's experience is below. I'm roughly twice their age and still working on myself, so please make clear this isn't a personal attack. If there aren't many jobs where they live, suggest working towards a move to a bigger city, remembering the higher costs. I want to reassure them that a first job not working out would be something to learn from.\n\n- Questioner describes little enthusiasm and wants minimal interaction at work.\n- Writer approximately twice questioner's age; still has personal changes to work on.\n- Questioner's education plans are unknown.\n- Some good jobs require little social interaction.\n- Bigger cities can have more jobs and higher living costs.\n- Close friend had similar social difficulties as a young person.\n- Friend chose door-to-door sales to practice communicating.\n- Friend still enjoys discussing that job's experiences and lessons.\n- Affordable education in an area of interest is valuable.\n- Early employment setbacks can teach useful lessons.\n- Self-improvement can expand job options.\n- Highly social work might be unpleasant at first and helpful later.\n\n(About me: forum participant offering career advice. Length: it should come to roughly 250-400 words.)",
  "hidden": {
